    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0065" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg18"/>

                <head>16. Telegram 250 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d16-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-08-02">August 2, 1955, 8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d16-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d16-1"/>
                <p>250. Some correspondents have learned from CHICOM newspaper sources CHICOMS gave
                    me “lists” at this morning’s meeting and will be carrying stories this effect. I
                    have closely questioned them and appears leak probably occurred before Wang had returned from meeting. Correspondents
                    say CHICOM group including press spokesman thus far scrupulously observing
                    secrecy agreement. I have assured correspondents if CHICOMS do not observe I
                    will give them backgrounder. They seem satisfied if not happy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
